  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather through this weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nNoreaster currently spinning about 250 miles south of Cape Cod\nas of 05z. At the same time a ridge of high pressure thru\nDowneast Maine courtesy of 1027mb sfc high over the Maritimes\nwill be keeping the area dry from coastal storm. 00z raob from\nKCAR indicates PW values only at 0.29 inches, approximately 10%\nof normal. Cold front dropping in from the north is moisture\nstarved and will likely only see clouds crossing the area as it\nmoves thru this afternoon. \n\nPressure gradient tightens in between noreaster and building\nCanadian high with north winds gusting upwards of 25-30 mph at\ntimes this afternoon, higher over Downeast and the higher\nterrain. \n\nHigh pressure building in Friday night with clear skies and\nwinds decoupling will lead to temps dipping into the 20s over\nthe entire area with perhaps some teens over the deeper valleys\nin the north. \n\nDry weather is expected through the weekend with an approaching\ncold front next Monday, though it looks moisture-starved as well.",
